  "description": "Creates a PaymentMethod object representing a customer's payment instrument (card, bank account, etc.). PaymentMethods can be: - Attached to a Customer for future use - Used directly with PaymentIntents to collect payments - Stored for recurring payments or subscriptions The 'type' parameter determines which payment-specific fields are required: - type='card': requires card object with number, exp_month, exp_year - type='sepa_debit': requires sepa_debit object with iban - type='us_bank_account': requires us_bank_account object with account details - And many other payment method types (acss_debit, au_becs_debit, bacs_debit, boleto, etc.) IMPORTANT: For card payments, collecting card numbers directly via API requires PCI compliance and special account permissions. Consider using Stripe.js, Stripe Elements, or mobile SDKs instead for better security and easier PCI compliance. This action is most useful for non-card payment methods or when you have explicit authorization for raw card data access.",
